                            %mover
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}_2 \times \mathbb{T}^d
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\mathbb{T}^d
                    \\\
                    (\sigma, \vec x)
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \- \vec x
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The resulting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕋
                      %mi d
                    %mo ⫽
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^d\sslash\mathbb{Z}_2
              has
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^d
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} mod
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\,,\, 1/2\, \mathrm{mod} \mathbb{Z}\}
            %p
              In applications to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              orbifolds of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕋
                      %mi d
                    %mo ⫽
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p,1} \times \mathbb{T}^d\sslash \mathbb{Z}_2
              play the role of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^d
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Op-planes"} Op-planes
          %h3#FlatCompact2DimensionalOrbifolds Flat compact 2-dimensional orbifolds
          %p
            In 2 dimensions the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystallographic+groups"} crystallographic groups
            are the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wallpaper+groups"}> wallpaper groups
            ”. Hence, as a special case of Example
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactFlatOrbifoldFromCrystallographicGroup"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            2-dimensional orbifolds may be classified as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-torus"} 2-torus
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wallpaper+groups"} wallpaper groups
            (for review see e.g.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Guerreiro09"} Guerreiro 09
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/CompactFlat2dOrbifolds.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#BettiolDerdzinskiPiccione18"} Bettiol-Derdzinski-Piccione 18
          %h4#TwoSphereAsFlatOrbifold 2-sphere
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            arises, in particular, as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}/\mathbb{Z}^2
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto -z
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+elliptic+function"} Weierstrass elliptic function
            (e.g.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Weierstrass+elliptic+function#Mukase04"} Mukase 04, end of 1.4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+orbifold"} flat orbifold
            with four singular points, called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pillowcase+orbifold"} pillowcase orbifold
          %h3#flat_compact_3dimensional_orbifolds Flat compact 3-dimensional orbifolds
          %h4#3sphere 3-Sphere
          %p
            Many flat compact oriented 3-dimensional orbifolds have coarse underlying topological space the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dunbar88"}> Dunbar 88
            )
          %h3#FlatCompact4dOrbifolds Flat compact 4-dimensional orbifolds
          %h4#kummer_surface Kummer surface
          %p
            The orbifold quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-torus"} 4-torus
            by the sign
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            on all four canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            is the flat compact 4-dimensional orbifold known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kummer+surface"} Kummer surface
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^4 \sslash \mathbb{Z}_2
            – the special case of Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoordinateReflectionOnNTorus"}
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BettiolDerdzinskiPiccione18"} Bettiol-Derdzinski-Piccione 18, 5.5
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/KummerSingular.jpg", :width => "300"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "orbifold#Snowden11"} Snowden 11
          %p
            Also
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^4\sslash\mathbb{Z}_4
            gives a toroidal orbifold. As
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D5-branes"} D5-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
            these are discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BuchelShiuTye99"} Buchel-Shiu-Tye 99, Sec. II
          %h4#4SphereAsFlatOrbifold 4-Sphere
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^2
            is an orbifold quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-torus"} 4-torus
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/213009/381"} this MO comment
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+elliptic+function"} Weierstrass elliptic function
            exhibits the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^2/\mathbb{Z}_2
            (
            %a{:href => "#TwoSphereAsFlatOrbifold"}> above
            ).
          %p
            A further
            = succeed "-quotient" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^2
            gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
            (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "4-sphere#AsAQuotientOfTheComplexProjectivePlane"} 4-sphere as quotient of complex projective plane
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#flat_compact_6dimensional_orbifolds Flat compact 6-dimensional orbifolds
          %p
            see
            %a{:href => "#FRTV12"} FRTV 12
          %h3#7dimensional_orbifolds
            7-Dimensional
            = succeed "-orbifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
          %p
            see
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-orbifold"} G₂-orbifold
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystallographic+group"} crystallographic group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branched+cover"} branched cover
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+orbifold"} complex orbifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+orbifold"} symplectic orbifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+orbifold"} Lorentzian orbifold
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            On 2- and 3-dimensional flat orbifolds (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+quotients"} orbifold quotients
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            by
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystallographic+groups"} crystallographic groups
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+H.+Conway"}> John H. Conway
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heidi+Burgiel"} Heidi Burgiel
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chaim+Goodman-Strauss"} Chaim Goodman-Strauss
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Symmetries of Things
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.routledge.com/The-Symmetries-of-Things/Conway-Burgiel-Goodman-Strauss/p/book/9781568812205"} ISBN:9781568812205
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+orbifolds"} Riemannian orbifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Joseph Ernest Borzellino,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Riemannian Geometry of Orbifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://digitalcommons.calpoly.edu/math_fac/111"} calpoly.edu/math_fac/111
            %li#Ratcliffe06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Ratcliffe"}> John Ratcliffe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric Orbifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foundations of Hyperbolic Manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-47322-2"} doi:10.1007/978-0-387-47322-2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://entsphere.com/pub/pdf/Ratcliffe%20-%20Foundations%20of%20hyperbolic%20manifolds%20(2e)%20-%20GTM%20149.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Christian Lange,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orbifolds from a metric viewpoint
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.03472"} arXiv:1801.03472
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10711-020-00521-x"} doi:10.1007/s10711-020-00521-x
            %li#BettiolDerdzinskiPiccione18
              %p
                Renato G. Bettiol,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrzej+Derdzinski"} Andrzej Derdzinski
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Piccione"} Paolo Piccione
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Teichmüller theory and collapse of flat manifolds
                %strong 197
                (2018) 1247-1268 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.08431"}> arXiv:1705.08431
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10231-017-0723-7"} doi:10.1007/s10231-017-0723-7
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+orbifolds"} Riemannian orbifolds
          %ul
            %li
              A. V. Bagaev &amp; N. I. Zhukova,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The isometry groups of Riemannian orbifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11202-007-0060-y"} doi:10.1007/s11202-007-0060-y
          %p Real-analytic Riemannian orbifolds:
          %ul
            %li
              Marja Kankaanrinta,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On real analytic orbifolds and Riemannian metrics
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/agt.2013.13.2369"} doi:10.2140/agt.2013.13.2369
          %p The Yamabe invariant:
          %ul
            %li
              Kazuo Akutagawal,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Computations of the orbifold Yamabe invariant
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00209-011-0880-0"} doi:10.1007/s00209-011-0880-0
          %p
            More generally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structures"} G-structures
            on orbifolds:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A. V. Bagaev, N. I. Zhukova ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The Automorphism Groups of Finite Type
                    = succeed "-Structures" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi G
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1022920417785"} doi:10.1023/A:1022920417785
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wolak"}> Robert Wolak
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orbifolds, geometric structures and foliations. Applications to harmonic maps
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.04190"} arXiv:1605.04190
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            and maybe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            on orbifolds:
          %ul
            %li
              Helio V. Fagundes, Teofilo Vargas,
              %em Orbifolds, Quantum Cosmology, and Nontrivial Topology
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0611048"}> arXiv:gr-qc/0611048
              )
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            on toroidal orbifolds
          %ul
            %li#BlumenhagenLustTheisen13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+L%C3%BCst"} Dieter Lüst
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Theisen"} Stefan Theisen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Toroidal orbifolds
              %em Basic Concepts of String Theory
              Part of the series Theoretical and Mathematical Physics pp 585-639 Springer 2013
          %p
            For more see the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
          %h3#flat_orbifolds Flat orbifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Ratcliffe"}> John Ratcliffe
              , Steven T. Tschantz,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Calabi construction for compact flat orbifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.topol.2014.09.005"} doi:10.1016/j.topol.2014.09.005
          %h4#of_dimension_2 Of dimension 2
          %p In 2 dimensions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
                ,
                %em On Lattès Maps
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0402147"}> arXiv:math/0402147
                )
            %li#Guerreiro09
              %p
                João Guerreiro,
                %em Orbifolds and Wallpaper Patterns
                (
                %a{:href => "https://faculty.math.illinois.edu/~ruiloja/Estudantes/TrabalhoJGuerreiro.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            2d toroidal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dongfeng+Gao"}> Dongfeng Gao
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kentaro+Hori"} Kentaro Hori
                %em On The Structure Of The Chan-Paton Factors For D-Branes In Type II Orientifolds
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.3972"}> arXiv:1004.3972
                ]
            %li#DMR14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+M%C3%A9ndez-Diez"} Stefan Méndez-Diez
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Geometrization of
                    = succeed "-Extended" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒩
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                %strong 22
                3 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09983"}> arXiv:1610.09983
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h4#of_dimension_3 Of dimension 3
          %ul
            %li#Dunbar88
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dunbar"}> William Dunbar
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric orbifolds
          %h4#of_dimension_4 Of dimension 4
          %p Flat (toroidal) orbifolds of dimension 4:
          %p
            In the the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
          %ul
            %li
              Justin R. David, Gautam Mandal, Spenta R. Wadia,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Microscopic Formulation of Black Holes in String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0203048"} arXiv:hep-th/0203048
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field+tadpole+cancellation"} RR-field tadpole cancellation
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            on toroidal orientifolds:
          %p
            Specifically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^4/G_{ADE}
            ) in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D9-branes"} D9-branes
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D5-branes"} D5-branes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Gimon"}> Eric Gimon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"} Joseph Polchinski
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Consistency Conditions for Orientifolds and D-Manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9601038"} arXiv:hep-th/9601038
            %li#GimonJohnson96
              %p
                Eric Gimon,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"} Clifford Johnson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em K3 Orientifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9604129"} arXiv:hep-th/9604129
            %li#BuchelShiuTye99
              %p
                Alex Buchel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Shiu"} Gary Shiu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anomaly Cancelations in Orientifolds with Quantized B Flux
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9907203"} arXiv:hep-th/9907203
            %li
              %p
                P. Anastasopoulos, A. B. Hammou,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Classification of Toroidal Orientifold Models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0503044"} arXiv:hep-th/0503044
          %p
            Specifically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
